uggled to attract  investors because they lack a  differentiating factor  now users of snapchat would likely  disagree with this statement given that  despite facebook and youtube's best  attempts to replicate the best features  of snapchat like stories most snapchat  users have preferred to continue using  snapchat for specific use cases  it seems like snapchat has mastered  casual conversations better than any of  their competitors but from an investor's  perspective who cares if snapchat  fulfills some niche role within young  adults lives on paper instagram is  superior in almost every way  for example in terms of demographics 18  to 24 year olds are snapchat's biggest  customer base and 13 to 17 year olds  make up nearly a quarter of their user  base meanwhile instagram's largest  demographic is 25 to 34 year olds with  second place going to 18 to 24 year olds  instagram's 13 to 17 year old base is  almost non-existent while the 35 years  knock demographic is actually quite  substantial if newer generations don't  switch over to using instagram that  could be a long-term problem but for the  time being instagram has no shortage of  users and all of their users are  significantly older than snapchat users  which means that they have more money  are more monetizable and are of course  more profitable this directly aligns  with household income studies conducted  on both platforms as well snapchat use  is most common amongst households with  income between 70 and 80 000 per year  meanwhile instagram use is most common  amongst households with incomes above  100 000 per year  again users with more money equals more  profits  something else to note about snapchat's  demographics is that it's mostly just  limited to the us  snapchat has 109.5 million users within  the us which is nearly more than all of  the users in all these countries  combined  if we take a look at instagram's usage  by country we can clearly see that it's  a lot more spread out especially amongst  emerging countries so from an investor's  perspective there's very little reason  to bet on snapchat over facebook if you  want to target millennials and older  instagram is the way to go  if you want to target people with money  instagram is the way to go  and if you want to target emerging  countries instagram is the way to go  the only reason to invest in snapchat is  if you think that younger generations in  the us will continue to use snapchat  over instagram which could very well be  true  but for this to become a financial  advantage for snapchat we'll likely have  to wait another 5-10 years at the very  least and in the meantime snapchat will  likely remain the underdog amongst  investors  aside from snapchat's unlucrative  demographic snapchat was also hit hard  with apple's privacy changes that rolled  out last year  if you guys aren't aware of this yet in  april of 2021 apple rolled out a feature  called the app tracking transparency  this feature allows users to choose if  they want to let third-party apps  collect data regarding their usage for  advertising purposes  and as you would guess basically  everyone opted out  according to this study only four  percent of americans were opting into  tracking and i have a feeling that a lot  of these guys may have accidentally  pressed allow snapchat's ceo evan  spiegel was actually a big proponent of  this move  in fact he believes that these privacy  changes were good for iphone consumers  and the social media ecosystem in  general  but despite his moral support for the  change this change was obviously not  good for snapchat's financials in  october of 2021 evan announced that  apple's privacy changes have actually  been affecting revenue more than they  originally anticipated and to make  things worse snapchat failed to meet  investors already conservative revenue  estimates which of course sent the stock  tumbling given this unfavorable  situation evan has chosen to focus on  profitability which he did accomplish  but this has left many investors  wondering at what cost sure it's nice to  invest in a profitable company but the  primary reason most snapchat investors  made the investment was because of  growth expectations and it now it seems  like evan is trying to piece investors  with profits instead of growth snapchat  doesn't have a p e ratio quite yet as  that requires a full year of  profitability but even if we take their  net income of 22.55 million dollars from  last quarter and extrapolated to a year  we only get about 100 million dollars  now this isn't a bad amount by any means  but compared to the market cap this  gives them a pe ratio of 673  even if we say that snapchat's  profitability grows to 250 million  dollars per quarter or 10x from where  they currently are their pe ratio would  still be quite high at 67.3 to put that  in perspective facebook's pe ratio is  under 20. this isn't exactly a bad thing  given that snapchat should theoretically  have a lot more growth left than  facebook but that's the key they need to  have growth and with apple's privacy  policy changes and potentially more on  the way investors aren't quite convinced  to give snapchat even more credit  at this point you may be thinking what  could possibly be worse than having  slower growth and a less profitable user  base  well the answer is being replaced  but wait a minute snapchat has a massive  user base most of whom are young so  snapchat won't be going anywhere anytime  soon right  well while that may be true that doesn't  prevent an old or new competitor from  overtaking snapchat  just take a look at tick tock tick tock  wasn't released till september of 2016  yet it was the most visited site in the  world in 2021  this isn't to say that it's easy to  replicate tick-tock success but it makes  it clear that the barrier for entry is  extremely low within the social media  industry from an app development  perspective it's not particularly hard  to create a social media app what's hard  is garnering users and 99.999  of social media apps will never garner  the same user base of snapchat or  facebook but from snapchat's perspective  only one or two of the millions of  social media apps out there need to  catch on for snapchat to lose user  engagement to these new apps and from a  user's perspective if a new better app  comes out the only thing stopping you  from switching over is your friends also  switching over  if your social circle switches over  you'll probably never look back and this  has been shown time and time again  within the social media industry  first there was friendster then there  was myspace then we had facebook and  twitter and after that we had instagram  and whatsapp and now we have snapchat  what's to say that snapchat won't  eventually be phased out as well  well the truth is that all companies are  eventually phased out it's just that the  phase at the top is rather short-lived  for social media companies due to the  low barrier of entry like apple for  example they also won't stay at the top  forever but think about how much more  difficult it is for a company to come  out with a smartphone and convince you  to pay several hundred dollars for it as  opposed to an app developer coming out  with a social media app and convincing  you to give it a shot obviously the  latter is magnitudes easier which is  great for competition and evolution but  not great for investors for example just  take a look at twitter stock they really  haven't moved in nearly a decade not to  mention it twitter has become  unprofitable once again and jack dorsey  has left the company  really the only social media stock that  has performed extremely well  historically is facebook and that's  mainly thanks to the acquisitions of  whatsapp and instagram also something to  note about facebook is that while they  have performed well financially they're  one of the most hated if not demoted  company in the world  so i don't think that's necessarily  something that snapchat should strive  for but at the same time if they don't  make acquisitions and become the big  tech company that everyone hates it's  just a matter of time until the new kid  on the block overtakes them anyway  while this video has mostly pointed out  the shortfalls of snapchat and the  social media industry i don't think  snapchat is going anywhere anytime soon  they just became profitable their user  base is just starting to make money and  there's still plenty of user growth left  for snapchat so i don't think snapchat  has really hit their stride yet meaning  that snapchat stock likely has a lot of  upside ahead but with that being said i  don't think snapchat is a lifelong hold  like many other investments such as the  s p 500 tesla bitcoin ethereum etc  whether snapchat peaks at a market cap  of 300 billion dollars or market cap of  a one trillion dollars i think it's just  a matter of time until they're phased  out and i think the next wave of facing  will be extremely painful i think the  next phase will not only be a move away  from snapchat but a move away from  traditional social media in general  with more people being aware of how  these companies make money and  increasing concern for privacy and more  backlash than ever before against big  tech i think it's highly likely that the  next big social media app will be some  sort of decentralized or non-profit  endeavor like signal i suspect mark  zuckerberg has similar beliefs and  that's why he cut back on social media  acquisitions and debating it all on the  metaverse with that being said i think  an investment into snapchat would be  more of a median horizon investment of  10 to 15 years you may be able to get in  make a solid 10x and get out but in my  opinion if you're gonna commit to a  stock for 10 to 15 years why not commit  to something that you can hold on to  life that can produce a 30 40 or 50x  return but that's just what i think  would you guys invest in snapchat  comment that down below  also drop a like if you use snapchat and  of course consider checking out our  international channels to watch their  videos in other languages and consider  subscribing to more questions logically  answered but until then i'm hari and  i'll see you guys on the next one  [Music]

